Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["Named Construction Samplers", "Title",
 CellID->509267359,ExpressionUUID->"4ddb5767-1f00-4973-a411-49eacd07850d"],

Cell["\<\
Synthetic constructions now have separate named samplers. The former public \
generic representative sampler is removed, with no compatibility alias.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"a19ecb8f-1463-48c4-b86d-7d434fcb4511"],

Cell["\<\
A token call preserves its declared carrier and sampling law. A bare \
half-line or infinite-line call retains its original traversal law; its token \
call samples the shortest-path DAG family. A bare regular polygon returns \
directed Graph legs; its token returns an ordered vertex sequence. A bare \
geodesic returns a position-spelled Graph; its token returns an ordered \
sequence.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"c754bcde-eefa-4016-848c-fd2e2c4a427a"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"With", "[", " ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", " ", 
    RowBox[{"graph", " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{"PathGraph", "[", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Range", "[", " ", "5", " ", "]"}], " ", "]"}]}], " ", "}"}], ",",
    "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"RandomInfraHalfLine", "[", " ", 
    RowBox[{"graph", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"InfraHalfLine", "[", " ", 
      RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", "3"}], " ", "]"}], ",", " ", "All"}], " ", 
    "]"}]}], " ", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[1]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"a2718fea-6f7d-454c-85c1-a5bcdf805ed1"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{"2", ",", "3", ",", "4", ",", "5"}], "}"}], "}"}]], "Output",
 CellLabel->"Out[1]= ",ExpressionUUID->"f3c6eaf7-2b35-4558-b93b-ee49e4077ae2"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"With", "[", " ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", " ", 
    RowBox[{"graph", " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{"PathGraph", "[", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Range", "[", " ", "5", " ", "]"}], " ", "]"}]}], " ", "}"}], ",",
    "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"RandomInfraBall", "[", " ", 
    RowBox[{"graph", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"InfraBall", "[", " ", 
      RowBox[{"3", ",", " ", "1"}], " ", "]"}], ",", " ", "All"}], " ", 
    "]"}]}], " ", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[2]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"fd87d2d4-0f83-4e46-9fec-016c36dde0c3"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{"2", ",", "3", ",", "4"}], "}"}], "}"}]], "Output",
 CellLabel->"Out[2]= ",ExpressionUUID->"7149844e-8d23-43d1-9b79-20e480fe37c9"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell["\<\
The old inert Ray, Line and Polygon spellings remain supported for this \
release. Their canonical names are InfraHalfLine, InfraInfiniteLine and \
InfraRegularPolygon. The old named ray and line samplers and predicates \
forward without drawing extra random numbers.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"d9fad0b0-4575-4711-b9a5-2f5bd7ccd850"],

Cell["\<\
Omitted or Automatic count selects one representative. An integer requests \
exactly that many distinct representatives, UpTo gives at most that many, and \
All enumerates the complete pool. Negative counts and unsupported options \
stay unevaluated. Default All and Identity do not advance random state. An \
explicit legacy stochastic selector retains its original action.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"dc4fa21e-742d-4834-803c-0d437305513f"],

Cell["\<\
Ball, Shell, Tube, Cylinder, Cone, SolidOfRevolution, BallHull, ConvexHull \
and Quadric each have one set representative, including an empty set. \
Intersection and Union sample points from complete operand supports. Point \
labels that are Lists remain intact.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"4df3fc99-756c-41c1-a0bd-b0c2e50e5393"],

Cell["\<\
The named functions are RandomInfraPoint, RandomInfraSegment, \
RandomInfraHalfLine, RandomInfraInfiniteLine, RandomInfraCircle, \
RandomInfraArc, RandomInfraRegularPolygon, RandomInfraPlane, RandomInfraBall, \
RandomInfraShell, RandomInfraSphere, RandomInfraTube, RandomInfraCylinder, \
RandomInfraCone, RandomInfraSolidOfRevolution, RandomInfraBallHull, \
RandomInfraConvexHull, RandomInfraQuadric, RandomInfraWalk, \
RandomInfraGeodesic, RandomInfraEllipse, RandomInfraIntersection, \
RandomInfraUnion, RandomInfraMidpoint, RandomInfraPerpendicularBisector and \
RandomInfraRegionNearest.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"c7b1bda1-e861-46cd-930d-318605b48760"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Exact Midpoint, PerpendicularBisector and RegionNearest are point families \
on finite simple undirected unweighted graphs. Their complete pools contain \
distinct raw vertices in graph order. Exact midpoint can be empty; \
equidistance does not imply separation; nearest support retains all ties. See \
",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["Synthetic geometry migration"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/tutorial/\
SyntheticGeometryMigration"},
   "RefLinkPlain",
   BaseStyle->{"InlineFormula"}]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "57bc6a6e-8dfa-488f-8d4f-04768af3a52b"],
 " for compatibility and the segment middle-layer distinction."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"ada74bc2-7da7-49bf-9afa-4b87ce4705b9"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"SeedRandom", "[", " ", "71", " ", "]"}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"With", "[", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"{", " ", 
     RowBox[{"graph", " ", "=", " ", 
      RowBox[{"CycleGraph", "[", " ", "4", " ", "]"}]}], " ", "}"}], ",", 
    "\n", "  ", 
    RowBox[{"InfraSubstrateHighlight", "[", " ", 
     RowBox[{"graph", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"InfraMidpoint", "[", " ", 
         RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "3"}], " ", "]"}], ",", " ", "1", ",", " ", 
        "3"}], " ", "}"}]}], " ", "]"}]}], " ", "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[3]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"acc62878-39f4-4d51-bdf7-51b5ab2e88fa"],

